<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PROBE C4. NEGATIVE CONTROL. What this asks: what happens when a BKM's @name
  and its <variable>/@name DISAGREE?

      businessKnowledgeModel @name = "f"
      its variable           @name = "g"
      the caller decision invokes  f(n)

  Section 6.2 states the invariant "BKM @name = variable/@name" and section 13.3
  row 6 measured the KIE side: validator ERROR, build clean, runtime FAILS. The
  Camunda side is one of the two gaps section 13.8 names by hand. This file
  measures both in one place and pins them.

  The cases assert the answer the file WOULD give if the names agreed (n * 3),
  so the probe distinguishes three outcomes rather than two: an engine may (a)
  refuse, (b) answer correctly anyway by preferring @name, or (c) answer null /
  wrongly. Only (a) and (c) make the invariant engine-checked; (b) means the
  emitter is on its own and checkDrg must carry it.

  Wired HarnessMustFail on the KIE leg. If it ever starts passing, KIE has
  changed its mind about the invariant and section 6.2 must be re-read.

  MEASURED 2026-07-31, and the engines DISAGREE, which is the point:

    KIE 8.44  : validator ERROR [VARIABLE_NAME_MISMATCH] "Variable name 'g' does
                not match the Business Knowledge Model node name 'f'"; BUILD
                CLEAN; and then at runtime, per case,
                    msg ERROR FEEL ERROR while evaluating literal expression
                    'f(n)': Not an invocable: 'null'
                with `result` reported FAILED and null. Section 13.3 row 6
                reproduced exactly.
    Camunda 8 : outcome (b). It PARSES, says nothing, and ANSWERS CORRECTLY
                (12 and 0). zeebe-dmn binds the invocable by the BKM's @name and
                does not consult variable/@name at all.

  CONSEQUENCE. Section 6.2's "@name = variable/@name" invariant is engine-checked
  on `kie` and completely unchecked on the DEFAULT flavor, where a mismatch is
  not merely tolerated but invisible. checkDrg must carry it. Wired
  HarnessMustFail on the KIE leg and HarnessMustPass on the Camunda leg.

-->
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" id="definitions_bkm_name_mismatch" name="bkm_name_mismatch" namespace="https://legalese.com/l4/dmn/bkm_name_mismatch" exporter="hand">
  <businessKnowledgeModel id="bkm_f" name="f">
    <variable id="bkm_f_var" name="g" typeRef="number"/>
    <encapsulatedLogic id="bkm_f_logic">
      <formalParameter id="bkm_f_p1" name="v" typeRef="number"/>
      <literalExpression id="bkm_f_lit">
        <text>v * 3</text>
      </literalExpression>
    </encapsulatedLogic>
  </businessKnowledgeModel>
  <inputData id="input_n" name="n">
    <variable id="input_n_var" name="n" typeRef="number"/>
  </inputData>
  <decision id="decision_result" name="result">
    <variable id="decision_result_var" name="result" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_result_n">
      <requiredInput href="#input_n"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <knowledgeRequirement id="kr_result_f">
      <requiredKnowledge href="#bkm_f"/>
    </knowledgeRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_result_lit">
      <text>f(n)</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
</definitions>
